    "name": "Recall private moments on a hotkey or scene trigger",
    "description": "Queue private memory recall for the next owned reply/swipe, or automatically match a real keyword or genuinely present character, then guide only the current native actor.\n\nSetup: Select Mara as the active native character and replace the canonical actor IDs everywhere. Create actor-private JSON mara-moments for Mara containing accepted Recall records, for example [{id:\"harbor-promise\",actorId:\"character:mara.png\",text:\"Mara remembers promising to return to the harbor.\",tags:[\"harbor\"]}]. This can also read Mara’s file produced by the paired-kiss recipe; remove/edit the tags filter to match your accepted records. Bind Prose for cast interpretation. Ctrl+R or the node context menu or Details Queue recall action queues a private request; then Send normally or request a genuinely new swipe. Hotkey target defaults both, uses one-per-type and consumeOn accepted: Apply spends that matching use, Stop/Reject leaves it unspent. Change target to reply/swipe/both, Repetition to Next matching generation, Once for each generation type or Until cancelled, and consumeOn to success or accepted deliberately. Default Recall activation Manual queue or keyword watches the real player message for harbor. For automatic character activation choose Manual queue or character presence and remove the obsolete player-source→recall.source wire; keep verified Presence. Manual bounded node Preview does not queue or inject. Native Recall currently serves only the selected active actor; switch actor and use their separately scoped workflow/file rather than recalling another actor’s private thoughts. Records are read from the live authorized file, never seeded as literal graph memory.\n\nInspect: On Send owns this generation. Generate Reply uses the ordinary SillyTavern connection. Auxiliary roles remain unassigned in this portable example. Review the final narrative and proposed consequences; Apply publishes a new swipe and settles staged writes. Preview and bounded runs never settle.\n\nGenerated suggestions are proposals. Quoted observations preserve source identity; notes never establish canonical events. Private records cannot be appended to public notes.",
